BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 605.77 Tm (Walker Deibel's most expensive lesson is the horizontal holding company. After running the family book) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 590.55 Tm (printer for seven years, Deibel bought six or seven companies across unrelated verticals at 80% to 100%) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 575.32 Tm (ownership with maximum debt, and the stacked risk turned uncorrelated businesses into correlated) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 560.10 Tm (problems; Deibel calls it the 'worst decision' and says eight companies in one vertical would have earned) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 544.87 Tm (multiple expansion instead [iYE-lc1tFUI @ 00:06:05]. Too many verticals is what ultimately made Deibel) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 529.65 Tm (stop acquiring [6KZrugmBkcs @ 00:34:19]. The margin trap is just as fast. Deibel calls margin 'the number) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 514.42 Tm (one most important thing' and reports a member who bought a sandwich business at 1% net margin and) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 499.20 Tm (was out of business within 90 days, with labor intensity, capital intensity and cyclicality stacking more danger) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 483.97 Tm (on top [AKE-710SdA4 @ 00:27:47]. People risk hits experienced operators too: at one company, 'at one) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 468.75 Tm (point 60% of my entire workforce walked out on me' [AKE-710SdA4 @ 00:33:19]. The fix is a one-vertical) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 453.52 Tm (playbook: buy one, focus on one, then add companies in the same space to capture the arbitrage, while) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 438.30 Tm (remembering that too many buyers in a sector kills it, exactly as the FBA aggregators showed.) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 423.07 Tm (Diligence misses are where buyers bleed quietly. Lucas Phillips paid for a quality of earnings report, yet the) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 407.85 Tm (time cards would have shown that nobody in the business worked 40 hours a week [iYE-lc1tFUI @) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 392.62 Tm (00:31:15]. A buyer named Joe nearly closed on earnings inflated by prepaid six- and twelve-month) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 377.40 Tm (contracts, and Deibel runs diligence in strict order, legal first for about a week, then financial, then) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 362.17 Tm (operational [u2bZWIf9b5k @ 00:53:33]. Trust failures are terminal: a friend bought a broom company from a) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 346.95 Tm (seller the friend did not trust and nearly went bankrupt, and Deibel's rule is to get out of there [6KZrugmBkcs) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 331.72 Tm (@ 00:42:18]. The paperwork phase kills deals too. The Master Afle summary of Deibel's book names) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 316.50 Tm (lawyers as the number one source of deals that fail to close and prescribes a not-to-exceed legal budget,) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 301.27 Tm (while Mark J Kohler warns that confirmatory diligence runs one to nine months, invites seller deal fatigue,) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 286.05 Tm (and that a half-page deal led straight to a lawsuit [eZBAyOccEhY @ 00:13:22]. Kohler's line is 'trust but) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 270.82 Tm (verify everything,' and Deibel adds that deals die one, two, three times before they close.) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 255.60 Tm (Post-close discipline separates survivors. Deibel's first acquisition closed with no plan, and the three-way) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 240.37 Tm (miscommunication between seller, general manager and owner 'destroyed value'; the fix is a person's name) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 225.15 Tm (next to every P&L line and meetings with the top 20 paying customers the week after closing) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 209.92 Tm ([WP5MdYhV05A @ 00:16:24]. Deibel also admits waiting too long to make changes on that first deal, and) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 194.70 Tm (warns against taking a CEO salary on day one because a debt-loaded business is 'overweight') Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 179.47 Tm ([aoPPGxWI8dY @ 00:00:29]. Expect everyone to hit you up for a raise once you own it. Run the economics) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 164.25 Tm (before signing: on $1M revenue with $150K SDE bought at 3x plus $100K of inventory, working capital and) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 149.02 Tm (closing costs, a 90% SBA loan means about $55K cash in and about $75K of annual principal and interest,) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 133.80 Tm (leaving the owner $75K [u2bZWIf9b5k @ 00:36:45]. Deibel puts the haggle in perspective: fighting over 3.2x) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 118.57 Tm (versus 3.5x is about 90 days of earnings on a 10-year loan, and buyers belong in $1M to $5M revenue) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 103.35 Tm (rather than sub-$1M shops [iYE-lc1tFUI @ 00:38:14]. Search itself is the biggest kill zone, since nine in ten) Tj ET
