BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 458.40 Tm (forensic money or a polite pass.) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 443.17 Tm (Owner compensation is the add-back everyone fights over, and practitioners price it in at least three different) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 427.95 Tm (ways. ProjectionHub warns that sellers routinely add back the full salary, say $100,000, when the buyer) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 412.72 Tm (must hire a $75,000 replacement to do the same job, so only $25,000 belongs in SDE, and even that figure) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 397.50 Tm (is a negotiation between buyer and seller [OiLlMiZv9ZQ @ 00:02:26]. The Finance Lab runs identical math) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 382.27 Tm (at middle-market scale, $900,000 of owner pay against a $350,000 replacement CEO for a $550,000) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 367.05 Tm (add-back, but attaches two conditions: the buyer must actually plan to hire at that salary, and the owner) Tj ET
